This product is an independent Rust port ("fork") of Rizzo Flow and includes material
derived from it:

  Rizzo Flow — https://github.com/Rizzo-AI-Academy/rizzo-flow
  Copyright Rizzo AI Academy
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  Ported / redistributed from Rizzo Flow:
  - the request and response JSON Schemas in schema/ (redistributed unmodified, so that
    clients see exactly the documented wire contract);
  - the behaviour of the decision, prompt, compat, calibration and evaluation modules,
    re-implemented in Rust (src/decisions.rs, src/prompts.rs, src/compat.rs,
    src/calibration.rs, src/evaluate.rs);
  - the ported test suite, derived from the original tests.

  The Rust port was written from the original sources; it is not a copy of the Python
  code, but it deliberately reproduces its contract and its behaviour.

The wire format implemented here matches the public "System One" interface described by
TypeSafe and named Jev in Rizzo Flow. It is used as an interface reference only: no
TypeSafe code or data is included in this repository.

Model weights are NOT distributed with this repository. The pinned GGUF used for the
measured results is downloaded separately from its publisher and remains under its own
license (the checkpoint used in the measurements declares Apache-2.0).
